<gpx version="1.1" creator="Flores Race Planner (pipeline/export_gpx.py)" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <name>S09 Sikka and the Portuguese south</name>
    <desc>Section 09 of the Flores Race traverse: Five centuries of Indo-Portuguese history, quietly kept. 86.7 km, +2447 m / -2431 m, starts at km 1054 of the course.</desc>
    <link href="https://github.com/technicaloutdoor/Flores-Race"><text>Flores Race Planner</text></link>
    <time>2026-09-05T06:27:58Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="-8.795162" lon="122.018125">
    <ele>6.4</ele>
    <name>Koka</name>
    <desc>km 0.0 | kind: checkpoint | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- Twin-bay beach on the south coast, reached via an ~8 km side road off the Trans-Flores highway near Paga. No lodging found; day-stop / checkpoint only. Coordinates from a single beach-tourism source; DEM confirms a coast</desc>
    <sym>Flag, Blue</sym>
    <type>anchor/checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.749412" lon="122.196971">
    <ele>13.2</ele>
    <name>Sikka</name>
    <desc>km 55.4 | kind: village | resupply: minimal | water: unreliable | sleep: homestay -- Seaside village on the south coast, seat of the old Sikka kingdom and site of the 1899 Portuguese-era church. Position corrected ~2.5 km to 'Gereja Tua, kampung Sikka' (the old church itself, Overture Maps place theme) -</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.720000" lon="122.166110">
    <ele>140.0</ele>
    <name>Lela</name>
    <desc>km 65.8 | kind: village | resupply: basic | water: unreliable | sleep: none -- Kecamatan capital between Sikka village and Maumere on the south-coast road; historic co-seat of the Sikka kingdom's Catholic mission. Coordinate is the Wikidata/GNS kecamatan centroid (139 m, a hillside position consist</desc>
    <sym>Residence</sym>
    <type>anchor/village</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.624377" lon="122.210411">
    <ele>24.8</ele>
    <name>Maumere</name>
    <desc>km 86.7 | kind: town | resupply: full | water: reliable | sleep: hotel -- Capital of Sikka Regency and the largest town of the eastern half of the island: market, ATMs, hospital (RSUD dr. TC Hillers), bike-ish parts, hotels. Frans Seda Airport is 5 km out (see p-frans-seda-airport). Rebuilt af</desc>
    <sym>City (Medium)</sym>
    <type>anchor/town</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.795162" lon="122.018125">
    <ele>6.4</ele>
    <name>Koka Beach</name>
    <desc>[anchor] Twin coves of pale sand and turquoise water separated by a small headland, ~8 km off the highway near Paga; one of the most photographed beaches on Flores' south coast.</desc>
    <sym>Beach</sym>
    <type>poi/beach</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.665969" lon="122.187054">
    <ele>214.9</ele>
    <name>Ledalero Seminary</name>
    <desc>[highlight] St Paul's Major Seminary, founded 1937 by the Divine Word Missionaries (SVD) on a hilltop ~9 km inland from Maumere; one of the largest Catholic seminaries in the world and a marker of how deeply Catholic this end of Flores is.</desc>
    <sym>Church</sym>
    <type>poi/religious</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.720000" lon="122.166110">
    <ele>140.0</ele>
    <name>Lela</name>
    <desc>[highlight] South-coast kecamatan capital between Sikka village and Maumere; a secondary seat of the old Sikka Catholic mission and a natural overnight/resupply link on the way into Maumere.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/heritage</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.766000" lon="122.056000">
    <ele>10.5</ele>
    <name>Paga Beach</name>
    <desc>[anchor] White-sand south-coast bay directly beside the Trans-Flores highway, roughly 50-60 km from Maumere; the course's arrival point on the south coast at the end of the Kelimutu/Lio section.</desc>
    <sym>Beach</sym>
    <type>poi/beach</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.749412" lon="122.196971">
    <ele>13.2</ele>
    <name>Sikka Old Church</name>
    <desc>[highlight, position approximate] Narrow wooden Baroque-style Catholic church built 1896-1899 by Pastor Yohanes Engbers with the Sikka king Yoseph Mbako Ximenes Da Silva; the best-known physical trace of Portuguese-era Catholicism on Flores' south coast.</desc>
    <sym>Church</sym>
    <type>poi/religious</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.749412" lon="122.196971">
    <ele>13.2</ele>
    <name>Sikka</name>
    <desc>[highlight] Seaside village on the south coast, capital of the pre-colonial Sikka kingdom from the 16th century and the point where Portuguese Catholicism first took root on Flores' south coast.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/heritage</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="-8.599703" lon="122.202836">
    <ele>7.2</ele>
    <name>Wuring</name>
    <desc>[highlight] Bajo (sea nomad) stilt village built out over the tidal flats at the edge of Maumere bay, a few km west of the town centre; one of Flores' few remaining Bajo settlements, passed on the way into Maumere.</desc>
    <sym>Museum</sym>
    <type>poi/traditional-village</type>
  </wpt>
